## 2. Screen domains before detailing the design

Perform a brief applicability screen for every project. Use the user's task, confirmed scope, actual data flows, and risks. Keep functionality within that scope. The [domain checks](domain-checks.md) expand PC, TC, KB, and SEC rules where their triggers apply.

For each domain, record the trigger fact and its location, applicability or uncertainty, affected objects, required depth and level, the existing design location, any gap, and the next action. Distinguish an unreviewed area, an uncertain trigger, and a capability outside the project scope. A small project can record a short reason for each absent trigger.

An applicable condition necessary to support a current claim is mandatory. A recommended method can change with a reason. An optional capability requires a project decision to adopt it. Match the depth of the record to actual consequences. A single passage may cover several related conditions if it retains their protection goals and applicable acceptance criteria.

## 3. Records and stop conditions

Retain the meaning of every necessary check under each rule. Use `CUSTOM:DOM01`–`CUSTOM:DOM08` for this supplement and preserve existing IDs. Cite the same source version when reusing evidence and state the scope it supports for each finding. Keep duplicate domain checks out of legacy PM/M and application acceptance denominators.

Record scope selection, applicability, check level and evidence result, user declaration, document confirmation, task readiness, and software execution separately. A parent condition is satisfied only when every required child condition has its required evidence. Keep unknowns, unavailable environments, failures, and unselected scope visible.

Block the actual dependencies of a critical unresolved item. Continue drafts, independent checks, and authorized actions where possible. Adoption requires a project decision. When adopted, establish the new baseline, compare its impact, and recheck the applicable scope. Preserve historical reports.

## 4. Project record template

Use the [domain check card](domain-check-card.md) in the existing document or a controlled appendix. Ordinary documents can use the existing authoritative text and record structure. The installed skill bundles these references.

The [domain checks](domain-checks.md) list the extent of external reading. FormSy designed the triggers, statuses, fields, and counterexamples for this supplement.
